<!--
    SystemUI corner padding for arcfox (Razr 50 Ultra).

      rounded_corner_content_padding  the horizontal padding SystemUI applies to
                                      the status bar so text and icons clear the
                                      curve (StatusBarContentInsetsProvider,
                                      KeyguardStatusBarView, ShadeHeaderController,
                                      NavigationBarView all read it)

    The corner RADIUS comes from the framework's rounded_corner_radius in
    core/res/.../config.xml; with this padding left at the AOSP default the
    corners are reported correctly but the clock is laid out as if the panel
    were square. That is why both files change together.

    Value read with aapt2 from Motorola's own overlay in the W1UXS36H dump,
    product/overlay/SystemUI__arcfox_g__auto_generated_rro_product.apk:

        dimen/rounded_corner_content_padding     27px

    The same overlay also sets dimen/real_rounded_corner_radius (103px). That
    name exists only in Motorola's SystemUI: no file in frameworks/base declares
    or reads it on lineage-23.2 or lineage-24.0, so it was dropped here rather
    than carried as an inert value.

    Deliberately NOT copied from the same overlay yet, because each needs its own
    verification and none of them is the reported bug:
      * config_enableDisplayCutoutProtection / config_frontBuiltInDisplayCutoutProtection
        (the camera-privacy ring drawn around the punch-hole)
      * cli_status_bar_height and the cli_* family, which belong to the cover
        display and are only meaningful once the cover panel is driven properly.
-->
<resources>
    <dimen name="rounded_corner_content_padding">27px</dimen>
</resources>
